      equipment: 'One standard pack of cards, one Joker, and a playing surface for the central trick pile.',
      dealing: 'The dealer distributes four cards to each player one at a time. The remaining cards form the face-down stock.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Lead: Dealer's left leads any card to start the trick. 2. Follow: Players must follow suit if they hold a card of that suit. 3. Draw: If unable to follow suit, draw one-by-one until a playable card is found. 4. Joker: Can be played anytime to win the trick; if led, the next player sets the suit. 5. Next: Winner of the trick leads the next one. 6. Page One!: Call 'Page One!' when down to one card.",
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Traditional Japanese Page One is a shedding game and does not utilize an ante or betting mechanism.',
      deal: 'Dealer only; performed once at start of the game.',
      reveal_market: 'This game does not feature a market zone or any market-based card acquisition mechanics.',
      buy_market: 'There is no system for purchasing cards from a market in the traditional Page One ruleset.',
      buy_stock: 'Players draw from the stock as a penalty or requirement rather than purchasing cards with currency.',
      fold: 'The game requires players to continue until their hand is empty; folding is not a valid action.',
      check: 'Betting rounds and the check action are not included in the traditional Japanese Page One game.',
      call: 'Standard betting calls are not used in this follow-suit shedding card game.',
      bet: 'Initial betting or wagering is not a component of the Page One shedding game loop.',
      raise: 'As there is no initial betting, raising the stakes is not an applicable mechanic in this game.',
      declare: 'Card combinations are not declared for points; see the Page One declaration for the shedding state.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands remain private and are only revealed card-by-card as they are played to the trick pile.',
      award_pot: 'There is no central pot of chips or currency to award at the end of the game round.',
      play_card: 'Must follow the suit of the lead card if possible; Joker may be played anytime.',
      draw: 'The standard draw action is replaced by the draw_until_playable requirement when unable to follow suit.',
      discard: 'Cards are played into a trick-taking format rather than being discarded into a common waste pile.',
      pass: 'Passing is not permitted; players must either play a card or draw until a playable card is found.',
      bid: 'Japanese Page One does not include an auction or bidding phase to determine a declarer or trump.',
      meld: 'There are no melding or set-matching mechanics where cards are laid down in combinations for scoring.',
      go_out: 'Must have only one card remaining and have correctly declared Page One to the other players.',
